@sanchit-gandhi I'm not proposing to replace it to `if not self.config.apply_spec_augment`. Making Wav2Vec2 `torch.compile()`-able is out of the scope of this PR. I just want to show that the problem that prevents Wav2Vec2 from being able to be compiled is due to the `getattr()` function, not due to overriding `return_dict`.

Let me know once your team has reached a decision regarding overiding `return_dict`.

On a separate note, I don't know how HF handles the config system, but it's kinda brittle to not be able to add new attributes to the config class in newer versions without resorting to call `getattr()`. There are definitely ways to handle that better. (Again, this is out of scope of this PR, I'm just commenting).
